<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see sun south, rain north.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see sun south, rain north.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Tuesday were forecast to see sun in the south and rain in the north, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see sun in the south rain in the centre and north with highs of 19 to 29 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see sun in the south and rain in the north with highs of 22 to 28 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see sun in the south and scattered showers in the north with highs of 28 Celsius.</p>
<p>((--Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
